<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23840" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-sīdo</span></b> , sēdi
			(<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>
			insidi, <i><span class="en">Amm. 28, 6, 4</span></i>), sessum,
				3, v. n. and <i>a.</i>, <i>to sit down in</i> or <i>on</i>, <i>to settle on;</i> constr. with dat.
				(<b>poet.</b> and post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apes floribus insidunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 708</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inscia Dido, Insidat quantus miserae deus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 719</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">volucres metuunt insidere ramis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					3, 407</span></i>
			. — With <i>acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 151</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apex insiditur astris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">littera "i" sibi insidit, coniicit enim est ab
					illo jacit,</span>”
				<i>coalesces</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 4, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">digitos membris,</span>”
				<i>sink into</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 257</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			partic., <i>to occupy</i>, <i>keep
				possession of</i> a place. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> With <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iniquis silvis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 11, 531</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			With <i>acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tumulos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
					24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aventinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 9,
					34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					21, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arcem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					26, 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">collem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					3, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad itinera insidenda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					24, 31</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fauces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					35, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saltus ab hoste insessus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 7,
					34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montes insessi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 13, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quo jugum melius aptum cervicibus insidat,</span>”
				<i>may sit more closely on</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 22, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to be fixed</i>, <i>remain</i>, <i>be rooted in</i>, <i>adhere to</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in memoria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de
					Or. 2, 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insedit in animo oratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tusc. 2, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tibi insedisset suspicio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Mil. 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">macula insedit in nomine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. de Imp. Pomp. 3</span></i>
			: dum illa verba memoriae insidant, <i>settle</i>, i. e. <i>remain fixed</i> or <i>rooted in the memory</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 10,
				7, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
